---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CitationBlock from "../../../components/CitationBlock.astro";
import PageIntro from "../../../components/PageIntro.astro";
import ScholarlyMeta from "../../../components/ScholarlyMeta.astro";
import SectionBlock from "../../../components/SectionBlock.astro";
import UseCaseFit from "../../../components/UseCaseFit.astro";
import { createImplementationPublication } from "../../../content/implementation-examples";

const pageTitle = "Retail personalization: implementation comparison";
const pageDescription =
  "Recommendation systems governed two ways: review gates, or an off switch, plus reasons and an answered challenge where targeting sets a price or an offer.";
const permalink = "/use-cases/examples/retail-personalization";
const anchorLinks = [
  { href: "#fit", label: "Where this fits" },
  { href: "#ethotechnics", label: "Ethotechnics implementation" },
  { href: "#citations", label: "Cite this page" },
];
const publication = createImplementationPublication(
  permalink,
  "Published the retail personalization implementation comparison.",
);
---

<BaseLayout
  title={pageTitle}
  description={pageDescription}
  publishedTime="2025-06-01T00:00:00.000Z"
>
  <PageIntro
    eyebrow="Implementation example"
    title={pageTitle}
    description={pageDescription}
    anchorLinks={anchorLinks}
  />

  {
    /* The page opened on "Where governance breaks down", which said what the
       boundary case says, then listed standard governance in a thin section
       of its own. Both are in the fit, which leads here instead of closing
       the page. */
  }
  <UseCaseFit slug="retail-personalization">
    <p>
      Personalization can quietly compound bias when users lack direct control
      over targeting loops.
    </p>
    <p>
      Standard governance relies on policy constraints and review gates with
      limited authority at runtime. It excludes sensitive attributes such as
      gender or age, runs cross-functional ethics reviews before deployment, and
      publishes notices about data use and tracking. A person oversees
      high-impact recommendation changes, and periodic audits look for
      demographic skew or unintended patterns.
    </p>
  </UseCaseFit>

  <SectionBlock
    id="ethotechnics"
    eyebrow="Ethotechnics implementation"
    title="What changes, and what to verify before launch"
    description="Where targeting sets a price, an offer, or who sees a job, it is treated as a decision about a person."
    variant="alt"
  >
    <div class="stack-sm">
      <ul class="card__list">
        <li>
          A person can turn personalization off, and it stays off. Turning it
          off does not cost them a price or an offer they would otherwise get.
        </li>
        <li>
          Where targeting sets a price, a credit offer, or who is shown a job,
          the person can see the main reasons it applied to them.
        </li>
        <li>
          A challenge to that price or offer goes to a named owner who answers
          by a stated date. That is what
          <a href="/glossary/contestability">contestability</a> means here.
        </li>
        <li>
          Upheld challenges are counted by targeting rule. The count goes to the
          rule's owner, who reviews the rule and records what changed.
        </li>
        <li>
          The owner can halt one targeting rule while it is reviewed, and a
          rollback target says how long it takes to undo a targeting change.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="muted">
        Before launch, publish the answer date for a challenge to a price or an
        offer. Measure <a href="/glossary/time-to-restore">time-to-restore</a> for
        mistaken targeting changes, and log each rollback in the repair log.
      </p>
    </div>
  </SectionBlock>

  <div id="citations">
    <CitationBlock
      title={pageTitle}
      permalink={permalink}
      publication={publication}
      summaryLabel="Cite this implementation example"
    >
      <ScholarlyMeta bare publication={publication} permalink={permalink} />
    </CitationBlock>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
